  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They didn't fold when the deficit hit three.",
    "what_this_means": "The lineup got runners on base thirteen times and converted six of them into runs, which is how you take a game you're trailing in and finish it on top by four. Ben Rice broke a tie in the seventh with a single. The moment that mattered most. But that single only worked because Chisholm and the rest had already done the hard work in the fourth, scratching out four runs when they were down. Max Fried exited after three innings with damage done, and the bullpen. Chivilli, Cruz, Headrick, Blackburn, and Doval all throwing clean. Gave the lineup room to work. This is a team that converts chances when they get them, and when the chances keep coming, that conversion rate is the difference between staying in it and going home. Rice gave them the go-ahead moment, but this was a balanced game where the broad offense made the bullpen's stability count.",
